            "custom_liquid": "<br>\n<div class=\"img_left\">\n<img src=\"https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0006/9969/5159/files/Vector_13.png\"></div>\n\n<div class=\"img_right\">\n<img src=\"https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0006/9969/5159/files/Vector_12.png\"></div>\n\n<style>\n#shopify-section-{{ section.id }} .img_left{\nposition: absolute;\nbottom: -80px;\nleft: -0px;\nwidth: 100px;\nopacity: 0;\n}\n#shopify-section-{{ section.id }} .img_left img{\nwidth: 100%;\n}\n#shopify-section-{{ section.id }} .img_right{\nposition: absolute;\ntop: -75px;\nright: 30px;\nwidth: 180px;\n}\n#shopify-section-{{ section.id }} .img_right img{\nwidth: 100%;\n}\n.img_left img, .img_right img{\nborder: none;\n}\n#shopify-section-{{ section.id }}{\n  overflow: hidden;\n}\n\n@media (min-width: 320px) and (max-width: 480px) {\n.shopify-section-{{ section.id }}-padding {\n    padding-top: 60px;\n    padding-bottom: 60px;\n}\n#shopify-section-{{ section.id }} .img_left{\nposition: absolute;\nbottom: -50px;\nleft: -10px;\nwidth: 50px;\ntop: unset;\n}\n#shopify-section-{{ section.id }} .img_right{\nposition: absolute;\ntop: -30px;\nright: -45px;\nwidth: 120px;\n}\n}\n</style>\n<script>\nwindow.addEventListener(\"load\", function() {\n\n  const section = document.querySelector('#shopify-section-{{ section.id }}');\n  if (!section) return;\n\n  const pageWidth = section.querySelector('.page-width');\n  const imgLeft = section.querySelector('.img_left');\n\n  if (pageWidth && imgLeft) {\n    \n    // Move after .page-width\n    pageWidth.after(imgLeft);\n\n    // Make visible\n    imgLeft.style.opacity = \"1\";\n\n  }\n\n});\n</script>\n<br>"
          }
        },
        "heading_YzDp3J": {
          "type": "heading",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "A FULL CIRCLE MOMENT",
            "heading_size": "h2"
          }
        },
        "text_zDGDqL": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>I grew up inspired by Pharrell and Chad Hugo. When I first heard “Grinding” at 11 years old, it shifted something in me. Around the same time, I discovered Ice Cream and Billionaire Boys Club after seeing Teyana Taylor modeling the brand. I started following the Ice Cream skate team and was heavily influenced by that early 2000s era. Watching skaters like Jimmy Gorecki and the rest of the team made me want to skateboard, dress like them, and be part of that world. It gave me direction during a time when I was a troubled kid, getting kicked out of schools and spending time in group homes. That culture opened my mind and made me want to create music and build something of my own.</p><p>Years later, I’ve come full circle — I now have a song with Chad Hugo. What started as inspiration turned into collaboration. That early Ice Cream and BBC influence still shows up in my work, including the colors and design of this K-Swiss sneaker. Jimmy was one of the original Ice Cream skaters, so having him involved in this launch felt natural. To me, he represents originality and authenticity, and it’s an honor to have him bring this project to life in his own way.</p>",
            "text_style": "body"
          }
        }
      },
